# Handbook sync adapter

This adapter keeps `personal/handbook/` (the bilingual derived documentation system)
consistent with the tree. It adds no workflow, axiom, or status semantics; the
policy is owned by `personal/handbook/_meta/sync-policy.md` and
`docs/standards/docs-sync-contract.md` §2/§5, and canonical governance sources
always win over handbook content.

1. **Route first.** Before finishing any change under `core/crates/`, `core/packages/`,
   `core/specs/`, `core/conformance/`, `core/tests/`, `personal/crates/`,
   `personal/apps/`, `personal/packages/`, `personal/tests/`, `personal/deploy/`,
   `tools/`, `.github/`, `.githooks/`, or the root manifests, match the changed paths
   against `personal/handbook/_meta/source-map.json` and update the mapped
   `doc_ids` in the same formal task and PR (both `en` and `zh-CN`).
2. **User-visible behavior** (CLI verbs/flags, configuration files, errors,
   security boundaries, installation, recovery) → update the affected
   `personal/handbook/*/user/**` and `personal/handbook/*/reference/**` pages.
3. **Architecture, data, protocol, authority, or test-environment changes** →
   update the affected `personal/handbook/*/developer/**` and
   `personal/handbook/*/ai/**` pages.
4. **Generated vs hand-written.** Pages with `generated: true` are refreshed only
   by `node tools/src/generate-handbook.mjs`; never hand-edit them. After editing
   a hand-written page or any file listed in its `sources:`, run
   `node tools/src/fill-handbook-fingerprints.mjs` (fingerprint drift is a CI
   red light, HB008).
5. **New tracked files** must match a rule in
   `personal/handbook/_meta/source-coverage.json` (owning docs, or an excluded
   category with a reason), otherwise `check-handbook` fails (HB009). New
   source-map globs must match at least one tracked file (HB015).
6. **No documentation impact** must be stated explicitly: pass
   `DOCS_IMPACT_NONE="<concrete reason>"` to the docs-sync gate and record the
   same reason in the commit/PR description. Blank or trivial reasons do not pass.
7. **Timing is mandatory.** The docs-sync gate
   (`node tools/src/docs-sync-gate.mjs --staged|--push`) runs before **every
   commit and push** — enable the repo hooks once per clone with
   `pnpm run hooks:install`; never skip it with `--no-verify`. Before flipping a
   task PR to ready, additionally run `node tools/src/check-handbook.mjs`,
   `node tools/src/generate-handbook.mjs --check`, and
   `pnpm run check:consistency`; CI enforces the same set on every PR.
8. **Canonical wins.** When a canonical source (governance, formal plan,
   `core/specs/`, `core/conformance/`, standards) conflicts with a handbook page,
   correct the handbook page in the same delivery — never "fix" the canonical
   source to match documentation. Never copy dynamic `PROGRESS.md`/Gate status
   into the handbook — link it (HB012).
